  "id": "cavalo_marinho",
  "name": "Cavalo-marinho (Pernambuco Zona da Mata folk drama)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Night-long folk drama of the sugar-cane Zona da Mata Norte of Pernambuco and neighbouring Paraíba, performed in the Christmas-to-Epiphany cycle, in which dozens of costumed figures, among them the Capitão, Mateus, Bastião and Catirina, play scenes between dances and sung loas; IPHAN has registered it as Brazilian cultural heritage. The music comes from the banco, a bench of musicians playing rabeca, pandeiro, bage (scraped bamboo) and mineiro (metal shaker), who also sing the toadas. The fiddle card stands in for the rabeca, a source-unspecified pandero for the pandeiro, the reco-reco for the bage and a source-unspecified shaker for the mineiro.",
  "recipe": "classic modern cavalo-marinho, groove Percussion, Brazilian branch. drone like fiddle, pandero source shaker source unspecified, bamboo reco reco. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
